# --- secondary_park ---
# Secondary hart parking loop. Non-primary harts spin here, polling the
# hart_mailbox word in the data section. When the primary hart (or the
# loaded program) writes a nonzero address to hart_mailbox, secondaries
# jump to that address. This allows the full node to wake up extra cores.

# ── secondary_park: ──
17 03 00 00 # LOAD_ADDRESS t1, hart_mailbox
13 03 83 11 # t1 = hart_mailbox ptr
0F 00 20 02 # fence r,r
83 22 03 00 # load mailbox value
E3 8C 02 FE # if zero -> keep waiting
67 80 02 00 # jump to target (full node takes over)

# --- Data Section ---
# Read-only data used by the bootloader:
# - b2s_iv: BLAKE2s initialization vector (8 x 32-bit words, RFC 7693)
# - b2s_sigma: BLAKE2s message schedule permutation table (10 rounds x 16 bytes)
# - b2s_g_idx: G-function call indices (8 calls x 4 byte indices per round)
# - expected_hash: 32-byte BLAKE2s hash of the expected binary
# - hart_mailbox: 4-byte shared variable for secondary hart wakeup

